DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbuuff__rriinngg functions provide a lock-less multi-producer and lock-less
     multi-consumer as well as single-consumer ring buffer.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__aalllloocc() function is used to allocate a buf_ring ring buffer
     with _c_o_u_n_t slots using malloc_type _t_y_p_e and memory flags _f_l_a_g_s.  The sin‐
     gle consumer interface is protected by _s_c___l_o_c_k.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__ffrreeee() function is used to free a buf_ring.  The user is re‐
     sponsible for freeing any enqueued items.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__eennqquueeuuee() function is used to enqueue a buffer to a
     buf_ring.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__ddeeqquueeuuee__mmcc() function is a multi-consumer safe way of de‐
     queueing elements from a buf_ring.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__ddeeqquueeuuee__sscc() function is a single-consumer interface to de‐
     queue elements - requiring the user to serialize accesses with a lock.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__ccoouunntt() function returns the number of elements in a
     buf_ring.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__eemmppttyy() function returns TRUE if the buf_ring is empty,
     FALSE otherwise.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__ffuullll() function returns TRUE if no more items can be en‐
     queued, FALSE otherwise.

     The bbuuff__rriinngg__ppeeeekk() function returns a pointer to the last element in the
     buf_ring if the buf_ring is not empty, NULL otherwise.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The bbuuff__rriinngg__eennqquueeuuee() function return ENOBUFS if there are no available
     slots in the buf_ring.

